<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fulwar Skipwith</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1765">1765</a>–<a href="/years/1839">1839</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fulwar Skipwith was an American diplomat and planter who was elected governor of the short-lived Republic of West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> in 1810. Earlier he had served as US consul in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> during the negotiation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana-purchase">Louisiana Purchase</a>. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> annexed the region at the end of 1810, he reluctantly yielded and later served in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a> legislature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fulwar-skipwith.jpg" alt="Fulwar Skipwith" width="280" height="380" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fulwar_Skipwith.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
